WEBVTT

00:00:03.237 --> 00:00:05.746
Memory needs a search index.

00:00:05.746 --> 00:00:09.287
Open Search, Indexes, and click Add index.

00:00:09.763 --> 00:00:12.934
Click Add on AI Memory for Elasticsearch.

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:18.263
The type for Azure AI Search works the same way, when that feature is on.

00:00:18.719 --> 00:00:23.349
Enter an Index Name, and a Name, which is how the index is listed.

00:00:23.836 --> 00:00:25.973
Pick the Embedding deployment.

00:00:25.973 --> 00:00:30.662
It turns each memory into numbers that the search compares, and it cannot

00:00:30.662 --> 00:00:32.976
be changed once the index exists.

00:00:33.472 --> 00:00:36.089
The other fields can stay as they are.

00:00:36.089 --> 00:00:39.182
Click Save, and the index appears in the list.

